cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ClusteringPro: finding, validating and interpreting natural groups in biological, ecological and agronomic data without programming"
abstract: >-
  ClusteringPro is a self-contained web application that performs a complete cluster analysis
  entirely in the browser, with no installation and no server-side computation. It guides the
  user from the raw table to publication-ready dendrograms and cluster maps: exploratory
  analysis and clustering tendency (Hopkins statistic, VAT), 39 similarity and dissimilarity
  coefficients for quantitative, binary, nominal, ordinal, mixed and ecological data, ten
  hierarchical linkage rules with an editable dendrogram studio and tanglegrams, k-means, PAM,
  CLARA, fuzzy c-means, Gaussian mixtures, DBSCAN and spectral clustering, thirteen criteria
  for the number of clusters with a consensus vote, bootstrap stability, multiscale bootstrap
  support of tree clusters, external validation, cluster profiling with test values and
  indicator species, discriminant analysis and classification rules, and an automatic report
  with a ZIP package of data, tables and figures.
